## 3. Data flow

The envelope crosses exactly two validation gates, both against this one file. Nothing
else in the system may accept a node document.

```
PAEOS goal seals at L16
   │
   ├─ L15 writes the emission bundle to the append-only outbox      (SAEOS-1 §6.1b)
   │     Decision · TradeOff · Option · Constraint · Component · Scar · EvidenceRef
   │     shape: INGEST profile — status=candidate, no confidence, no promotion,
   │            no lifecycle, no review_priority
   ▼
SAKG ingest pulls (never push)
   │
   ▼
┌─ GATE 1 ── validate @ envelope.schema.json#ingest ───────────────┐
│  reject → ingest defect, node never enters the corpus            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   │ accept
   ▼
Store materializes the node:
   • computes confidence            → confidence + confidence_derivation
   • records frequency, if any      → review_priority   (priority only, never promotion)
   • assigns corpus_seq
   ▼
┌─ GATE 2 ── validate @ envelope.schema.json  (root = #stored) ────┐
│  reject → store defect (the store built a malformed node)        │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   │ accept
   ▼
Corpus  ◄── Truth Maintenance: on any Outcome/edge change, recompute confidence,
   │        bump corpus_seq, re-run GATE 2. Propagates along derived_from / supports.
   │        Later: L17/L19 emits an Outcome node bound to the Decision (Ω2 loop).
   ▼
Projection (§5.1) — SUMMARY tier emits only { id, label, summary, status, confidence }
   ▼
Consumer context, tagged provenance: sakg · tier: SUMMARY|INDEX · trust: untrusted
```

**Element-by-element.** Every envelope field is produced at exactly one place and consumed
at at least one — no orphan:

| Field | Produced by | Consumed by |
|---|---|---|
| `id`, `type`, `namespace` | producer at emission | addressing, tenancy filter (Ω5), all five §5.2 methods |
| `label`, `summary` | producer | the SUMMARY/INDEX projection unit (Ω3) |
| `facets` | producer | type-specific traversal (`Scar.detection_signature`, `TradeOff.axis`, …) |
| `coordinates` | producer | `analogous_to` / cross-domain transfer (✓9), disclosure scoping |
| `provenance.*` | producer at emission | FPL-7 re-verify-or-discard; `why` path in the projection response |
| `evidence[]` | producer (hashes only) | promotion gating; consumer re-verification against PAEOS CAS |
| `status` | store (transition guard) | `filters.status`, default `[canonical]` (§5.1 r4) |
| `confidence` + `confidence_derivation` | **store only** | `filters.min_confidence`; withheld below threshold (§7) |
| `valid_from` / `valid_until` | producer / store on supersession | `filters.as_of` time travel (Ω4) |
| `falsifier` | producer | the refutation watch (Ω4/K6) |
| `promotion` | store at promotion | audit of ×5 compliance |
| `lifecycle` | store at terminus | retention proof; lineage walk |
| `review_priority` | store, from ingest frequency | human/agent review queue ordering — **never** the projection ranking authority |

**Sensitivity.** The envelope carries no artifact bodies and no evidence results (DD-5), so
a leak across a namespace boundary discloses labels, summaries and hashes — not source. The
disclosure policy that governs cross-namespace edges (Ω5) is a later slice (S5); this
schema's contribution is that `namespace` is mandatory and pattern-bounded from day one, so
no node can exist untenanted.

