## 8. Validator obligations — checks a schema provably cannot carry

Stated so the seam is visible and nothing is silently assumed covered. Each has a named
downstream owner; none is a gap in *this* goal.

| id | Obligation | Why not schema-expressible | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| **R1** | `id`'s embedded `<namespace>` and `<Type>` equal the `namespace` and `type` fields | cross-field equality | ingest validator |
| **R2** | `promotion.evidence_hash` ∈ `{evidence[].hash}` | cross-field membership | ingest validator |
| **R3** | `valid_until` ≥ `valid_from`; `lifecycle.terminated_at` ≥ `valid_from` | cross-field ordering | ingest validator |
| **R4** | Transition legality (no `refuted → canonical`, no demotion) | needs the prior state | transition guard |
| **R5** | Nothing is ever deleted, at *corpus* scope | needs two corpus snapshots | append-only store + corpus-diff check |
| **R6** | `evidence[].hash` resolves in PAEOS CAS and re-verifies | needs the outside world | consumer, on re-verification (FPL-7) |
| **R7** | Dependency edges acyclic within a namespace (§4.4) | edge-level, not node-level | edge-schema goal |
| **R8** | Cross-namespace disclosure policy (Ω5) | policy state outside the node | slice S5 |

